gotiation models", "children": [{"id": "4104f90b-db26-4d82-b81f-2e15e1298370", "type": "concept", "title": "distributive bargaining"}, {"id": "852f2b7c-eee0-42c1-8322-ac8ee1b0d78e", "type": "concept", "title": "integrative bargaining"}, {"id": "908d042f-c1a5-43ca-8df3-33c8b1bfd33f", "type": "concept", "title": "interest-based bargaining"}, {"id": "d4c34bb0-3b24-459d-8b72-0327c994e9c3", "type": "concept", "title": "package proposals"}, {"id": "4a5b6f76-cd6e-4740-9268-c9fc22d94a25", "type": "concept", "title": "concession patterns"}], "description": "The class compares positional bargaining, interest-based bargaining, and hybrid approaches."}, {"id": "8b30e8fe-fd31-4816-9ba6-58ab444fd068", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Impasse and settlement", "children": [{"id": "b0d3f624-927b-4383-b815-4c56ce50cdb6", "type": "concept", "title": "good-faith bargaining"}, {"id": "720a91cf-9244-483d-8b37-2e769633f62f", "type": "concept", "title": "impasse"}, {"id": "d08b9e35-6358-4db0-a16e-71cdc0ccef34", "type": "concept", "title": "last best offer"}, {"id": "8f66fa65-75b4-476f-a6c4-ac6a705bbbca", "type": "concept", "title": "tentative agreements"}, {"id": "a97cb896-8467-4853-8c57-1e53c404d086", "type": "concept", "title": "ratification"}], "description": "Students learn the legal and strategic meaning of impasse, tentative agreements, ratification, and implementation."}]}, {"id": "cc7d36fa-c9bb-425d-8d9b-577dfd082a13", "type": "topic", "title": "Bargaining Data, Compensation, Benefits, and Contract Costing", "description": "Students learn to put numbers behind bargaining strategy so proposals are financially credible and operationally realistic.", "children": [{"id": "23cf8ccb-e107-4dff-8352-1ee7d181ee1e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Wage and benefit costing", "children": [{"id": "0be1b6ea-8017-4243-a875-0bd709258695", "type": "concept", "title": "base wage rates"}, {"id": "7899b930-9644-440f-a870-cf1057e7b753", "type": "concept", "title": "step systems"}, {"id": "97d6f705-5eaa-47c3-b68c-e3fa538b8574", "type": "concept", "title": "shift differentials"}, {"id": "bece5dd6-d224-4602-b552-bfbbc17b4064", "type": "concept", "title": "health premiums"}, {"id": "6cfc9665-83b5-46b2-b81e-40ca130faf8f", "type": "concept", "title": "pension contributions"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches students to calculate the cost of wage increases, premiums, health benefits, and retirement proposals."}, {"id": "ab44308c-e4df-4c69-873e-d30a89bc4f48", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparables and affordability", "children": [{"id": "60f99fda-31d1-452d-9001-a95d0d5c5312", "type": "concept", "title": "external comparables"}, {"id": "28b30568-bd3c-49d1-aa1d-21db38eee519", "type": "concept", "title": "internal equity"}, {"id": "2fee4753-c67d-4f03-aad1-fa5805a83043", "type": "concept", "title": "ability to pay"}, {"id": "3908e8e0-1c77-40ca-a8dd-03e45efdca60", "type": "concept", "title": "budget constraints"}, {"id": "5bb0ac7d-97ea-4cc7-a09b-8f728c6dfa4d", "type": "concept", "title": "cost-of-living measures"}], "description": "Students learn how parties use market comparisons, budgets, revenue, profitability, and public-sector fiscal limits."}, {"id": "9e4fb9f1-4829-40d5-b8fd-c05458c7dc7f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data ethics and transparency", "children": [{"id": "5485c4b7-a5d2-4eb7-8be9-903ceb0cbcc6", "type": "concept", "title": "information requests"}, {"id": "3727bc1d-6d34-4eaa-be29-9b0859e4dd17", "type": "concept", "title": "confidentiality"}, {"id": "11a4e31a-bdcc-4eaf-86bc-33bafac12da4", "type": "concept", "title": "data accuracy"}, {"id": "590178d4-a1f8-46ee-a90c-a65a55d03578", "type": "concept", "title": "cost assumptions"}, {"id": "e5972277-6f84-438f-bad3-2b4505620e8e", "type": "concept", "title": "trust in numbers"}], "description": "The class examines how selective data use, confidentiality, and trust affect negotiations."}]}, {"id": "f55beef1-4260-4f20-ae7c-347746b27fb9", "type": "topic", "title": "Contract Language, Administration, and Workplace Implementation", "description": "This section shows how collective bargaining agreements become daily workplace governance systems.", "children": [{"id": "48d40e21-f11c-43b9-9ecc-2c01fb544436", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Core contract clauses", "children": [{"id": "6b7a1fcd-0a44-4614-8fcc-e022e8501a1a", "type": "concept", "title": "recognition"}, {"id": "4f62d44a-c5fb-4e1e-a079-6daf19d06f8e", "type": "concept", "title": "management rights"}, {"id": "c6c300f8-86e1-4af0-a2da-7dc6291c9c57", "type": "concept", "title": "union security"}, {"id": "a3377408-22ec-4bfe-b704-25f32081de71", "type": "concept", "title": "seniority"}, {"id": "b43020f6-5f71-449d-acd9-e84f5c4e30d4", "type": "concept", "title": "no-strike clauses"}], "description": "Students learn the meaning and tradeoffs in common collective bargaining agreement provisions."}, {"id": "e23b9cb1-3ad5-4adc-8b61-018d8293e094", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Work rules and operations", "children": [{"id": "6e288cf9-dc49-4ccc-9c23-5a927ab066b8", "type": "concept", "title": "scheduling"}, {"id": "9e20edf9-e302-4023-98b2-9a9f4d979bca", "type": "concept", "title": "overtime distribution"}, {"id": "ab875302-ac1e-481f-9f43-b1dc0fa70998", "type": "concept", "title": "job bidding"}, {"id": "c8de656f-147f-4147-816b-f5c4ce3ed36a", "type": "concept", "title": "subcontracting"}, {"id": "0c7dc1db-1e89-411f-814b-fd57f5e4aed8", "type": "concept", "title": "safety committees"}], "description": "The class connects contract language to scheduling, overtime, classification, subcontracting, safety, and discipline."}, {"id": "6039f1da-c4c9-4050-a9db-a3e73780bd65", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Administration systems", "children": [{"id": "66c8f870-766e-4d58-b50b-5b1752f2c44e", "type": "concept", "title": "contract interpretation"}, {"id": "927a8c75-596f-46a5-b5a3-9706cf2d781e", "type": "concept", "title": "past practice"}, {"id": "769052a9-098a-45e2-b1e0-162876f62220", "type": "concept", "title": "labor-management meetings"}, {"id": "aedf6c71-b630-4b51-8ff3-8381fb1fa5ee", "type": "concept", "title": "supervisor training"}, {"id": "26d58a33-be85-4478-a0ba-2dd486ee8260", "type": "concept", "title": "documentation"}], "description": "Students learn how HR, supervisors, stewards, and managers keep contract implementation consistent."}]}, {"id": "35428132-60b9-4af9-b4d6-3c9154bf860b", "type": "topic", "title": "Grievance Handling, Just Cause, and Arbitration", "description": "Students learn how workplace disputes are processed, documented, argued, and resolved under a collective bargaining agreement.", "children": [{"id": "a4b02877-c642-460b-b93e-73fc685b962e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Grievance procedure", "children": [{"id": "19e356ec-36e2-40cc-acdf-ef47c3429a4f", "type": "concept", "title": "filing timelines"}, {"id": "a7c900fa-178d-40b2-8d2c-773cdde8a02d", "type": "concept", "title": "step meetings"}, {"id": "2f2e6361-9394-4dc7-9bf5-edc9d7d8792f", "type": "concept", "title": "steward roles"}, {"id": "ca4dd110-f9d3-401c-baf5-ee6165f30989", "type": "concept", "title": "settlement authority"}, {"id": "f7efacd8-1314-405e-b89f-2b02510e9a23", "type": "concept", "title": "withdrawals"}], "description": "This subtopic maps the steps, timelines, parties, and evidence needed to process grievances well."}, {"id": "b327e95e-04bd-43d5-92a1-85304cae285e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Just cause and discipline", "children": [{"id": "8e9723e4-108d-403d-8f31-0d0d2d43f9f1", "type": "concept", "title": "notice"}, {"id": "3dd520d6-3d0b-4226-b8dd-7db8df34dc8d", "type": "concept", "title": "reasonable rule"}, {"id": "7aedff20-d9a4-4b14-b070-5f17bdde8c84", "type": "concept", "title": "investigation"}, {"id": "22092efe-60d7-43eb-a874-de3174684cc8", "type": "concept", "title": "proof"}, {"id": "9e88cfdd-9607-4d8a-9db5-9a7758a7567b", "type": "concept", "title": "proportionality"}], "description": "Students learn the fairness standards arbitrators use to evaluate discipline and discharge."}, {"id": "619733a1-4965-488f-b206-05cc17366a8c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Arbitration advocacy", "children": [{"id": "5153e8a4-9a9b-4d21-90a7-e117b4131e13", "type": "concept", "title": "opening statements"}, {"id": "8c497143-4b6f-481d-865c-a6d067dd8b84", "type": "concept", "title": "witness preparation"}, {"id": "63b4d1aa-844f-420b-92d3-172d81f5eb05", "type": "concept", "title": "document evidence"}, {"id": "d53d6272-c4f5-4ad1-85b8-7a5f6647a29e", "type": "concept", "title": "arbitrator authority"}, {"id": "827c1e27-1fba-4433-9bcd-7dd8d03a16f9", "type": "concept", "title": "make-whole remedies"}], "description": "The class introduces hearing preparation, evidence, witnesses, briefs, awards, and remedies."}]}, {"id": "113a14b9-3a95-40d1-bc03-bfcfaa92bbcc", "type": "topic", "title": "Strikes, Lockouts, Impasse, Mediation, and Dispute Resolution", "description": "This unit teaches students how conflict escalates and how skilled labor-relations professionals prevent, manage, or resolve breakdowns.", "children": [{"id": "651735c9-c087-4837-ad54-e82640ef845e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Economic weapons", "children": [{"id": "ce75738e-c2e7-4360-9e4a-d7fddf4f9050", "type": "concept", "title": "economic strikes"}, {"id": "847f8f86-5f39-4ed4-b83a-8eada6dfeac0", "type": "concept", "title": "unfair-labor-practice strikes"}, {"id": "4ead4e30-cfc4-41bd-9c1c-33b3344e084c", "type": "concept", "title": "lockouts"}, {"id": "c489ec6b-e409-4095-a6fe-a1a8a6b3f343", "type": "concept", "title": "picketing"}, {"id": "2362ce71-5b9a-4aab-b6d4-dcde72b7c701", "type": "concept", "title": "replacement workers"}], "description": "Students learn the legal and strategic role of strikes, lockouts, picketing, boycotts, and replacement workers."}, {"id": "fd8347f4-418f-4832-9438-034fc830a405", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Third-party dispute resolution", "children": [{"id": "bb7455e5-2cde-4a20-b158-d6d3e5d6b611", "type": "concept", "title": "FMCS mediation"}, {"id": "71a70d73-4a0e-495b-9603-8f0faf79c241", "type": "concept", "title": "fact-finding"}, {"id": "719b769d-0721-4830-82a1-ee9da683d64e", "type": "concept", "title": "interest arbitration"}, {"id": "ce7c880e-a4a3-46a7-9d82-cbe5c3f4518a", "type": "concept", "title": "conciliation"}, {"id": "8096b4b4-f488-4d47-99fd-47a44310efa4", "type": "concept", "title": "cooling-off periods"}], "description": "The class covers mediation, fact-finding, interest arbitration, and other tools for breaking impasse."}, {"id": "530cb5ea-0f16-4a3e-a1cf-464ed7c5e8f9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Strike preparation and settlement", "children": [{"id": "834ab33e-eec6-43e2-8bf8-de16b3c15cfe", "type": "concept", "title": "contingency planning"}, {"id": "c9c593c6-49f4-4e54-a910-8f7b7eb3b9a5", "type": "concept", "title": "strike funds"}, {"id": "6343e06f-d081-4666-a385-4d2a2be5083c", "type": "concept", "title": "communications"}, {"id": "4abe87b4-78ef-4111-85e8-d775042b6c57", "type": "concept", "title": "return-to-work agreements"}, {"id": "69678c8f-778a-4f73-9f15-394bb4ce828c", "type": "concept", "title": "rebuilding trust"}], "description": "Students examine operational, legal, communication, and relationship issues during high-conflict bargaining."}]}, {"id": "dbf7c7e3-9aa4-4e33-a8db-4304794dd21f", "type": "topic", "title": "Public-Sector Labor Relations", "description": "Students learn why public-sector bargaining differs from private-sector bargaining because the employer is also a government entity accountable to voters, budgets, and essential services.", "children": [{"id": "44521919-4bdb-48b3-a22e-3fa94cd63f1c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Public-sector legal frameworks", "children": [{"id": "6e28b1a4-f70c-45ce-a49c-7ee7cecf7b00", "type": "concept", "title": "state bargaining statutes"}, {"id": "a0f33c90-3991-4664-84d7-0152a38061a2", "type": "concept", "title": "federal-sector labor law"}, {"id": "d30890ec-07e4-4647-bfcb-0dadf1a1a905", "type": "concept", "title": "scope of bargaining"}, {"id": "e4f88261-709a-43e1-a1a0-93e5f82f78f7", "type": "concept", "title": "management rights"}, {"id": "854a55a0-c41e-4955-8332-35d7f5867714", "type": "concept", "title": "essential employees"}], "description": "This subtopic compares federal, state, and local bargaining systems."}, {"id": "80738a79-e9c4-4749-8753-feb5a2ea2461", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Budgets and politics", "children": [{"id": "e2a223f4-cde5-4d2f-ae7f-bbe14965036b", "type": "concept", "title": "appropriations"}, {"id": "a4ce6079-ea95-4266-8a60-b9a2e29d90e7", "type": "concept", "title": "tax constraints"}, {"id": "a720db7f-b685-4b06-b441-51e951140151", "type": "concept", "title": "public hearings"}, {"id": "f1363bba-0440-4e52-b747-37ae96cfac46", "type": "concept", "title": "elected officials"}, {"id": "56706df9-167d-4bf8-bab7-dab5e924e9dc", "type": "concept", "title": "transparency"}], "description": "Students learn how political oversight, tax revenue, public opinion, and budget cycles shape bargaining."}, {"id": "f8ec4b55-a056-44de-8619-b0361e7b9926", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dispute resolution in essential services", "children": [{"id": "a2e070f5-f0a0-4623-83a5-9e286fc29d6e", "type": "concept", "title": "strike bans"}, {"id": "3ce6dd1b-f5c8-4d8f-bcc7-a51115581ccf", "type": "concept", "title": "mediation"}, {"id": "cd94da28-f22e-4aed-9d47-e882776eee0e", "type": "concept", "title": "fact-finding"}, {"id": "2a651511-4cf3-40f8-b378-498c6ac5e213", "type": "concept", "title": "interest arbitration"}, {"id": "d377d524-c5e9-43ec-a2e9-e834750b89ae", "type": "concept", "title": "essential-service continuity"}], "description": "The class covers strike restrictions and alternatives used for public safety, education, transit, and health services."}]}, {"id": "a0558bde-5b1c-4a1f-9488-0b0b2219edd2", "type": "topic", "title": "Labor-Management Partnership, High-Road Work Systems, and Change", "description": "This section shows that labor relations is not only conflict management; it can also support productivity, safety, innovation, and shared problem-solving.", "children": [{"id": "c62a5ff7-cc48-4db2-bb43-fcfdee3286b9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Partnership structures", "children": [{"id": "aff036a2-6e14-43a9-8e62-2405ba4f43c8", "type": "concept", "title": "joint committees"}, {"id": "af8a8f50-1bbb-4a9a-b2e3-c44a38d37563", "type": "concept", "title": "charters"}, {"id": "ec533013-8c8d-42fe-9b29-62cf70c4f67a", "type": "concept", "title": "agenda setting"}, {"id": "8a3fdc79-6d8b-448b-8740-36eca288a66c", "type": "concept", "title": "decision rights"}, {"id": "180a113d-78ad-4a3b-a8b4-0e637060286f", "type": "concept", "title": "metrics"}], "description": "Students learn how joint committees and labor-management forums are designed and governed."}, {"id": "d46ef411-9655-4f99-a102-2012e24d5c44", "type": "subtopic", "title": "High-road work systems", "children": [{"id": "c7b8e181-cac7-4d8c-8fa1-3b7ab97d264c", "type": "concept", "title": "skills training"}, {"id": "b996fe6f-02ad-4866-91c9-bad0ee784afc", "type": "concept", "title": "career ladders"}, {"id": "6db1b4ae-1029-4dfd-a70b-263e68874347", "type": "concept", "title": "participation"}, {"id": "dbff56be-4c1c-4be0-8fbb-4cf6a2c8334e", "type": "concept", "title": "quality improvement"}, {"id": "8cfc0b8a-cdc3-4204-b56d-9695606fe8dc", "type": "concept", "title": "job security"}], "description": "The class explores strategies that link worker voice with training, quality, safety, and operational improvement."}, {"id": "64c3875e-70c9-407c-9f0e-3c377b93c511", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Technology and change", "children": [{"id": "5b4fc510-0ec2-4a58-8f2f-7bc24f79104d", "type": "concept", "title": "effects bargaining"}, {"id": "e67a692b-d831-4805-a98e-516471a044c6", "type": "concept", "title": "automation"}, {"id": "174f6216-2bc3-4207-9e0f-d47b60059644", "type": "concept", "title": "AI monitoring"}, {"id": "ed2fd189-06f1-4df9-83ba-d0d54796b85a", "type": "concept", "title": "reskilling"}, {"id": "60d1840b-be39-43f2-a073-659a2beb1f85", "type": "concept", "title": "change communication"}], "description": "Students learn how automation, scheduling systems, AI, and restructuring become bargaining and implementation issues."}]}, {"id": "88935cfb-41fa-4e2c-b00c-6bcb987a00a5", "type": "topic", "title": "Comparative Labor Systems and Global Supply Chains", "description": "Students broaden their perspective by comparing U.S. labor relations with international and transnational models of worker representation.", "children": [{"id": "5a19c569-01e5-45fa-936b-46e27c530fb1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparative institutions", "children": [{"id": "90df4a53-6bd6-4d5b-9083-5d877d18a1c0", "type": "concept", "title": "sectoral bargaining"}, {"id": "9bd94091-fcb5-4fdd-8fb2-1dc3253475ac", "type": "concept", "title": "works councils"}, {"id": "fc1e0f6e-3920-4b3e-8a87-8f73feb9dcc1", "type": "concept", "title": "codetermination"}, {"id": "b1497960-ac93-4be8-ac9c-ace75b12e040", "type": "concept", "title": "social partnership"}, {"id": "05333efd-f184-4595-bf00-bfa3634022ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Ghent systems"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces institutions that differ from U.S. enterprise-level bargaining."}, {"id": "accb0eae-0fbc-4c63-9e25-d1f573f6aad1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global labor standards", "children": [{"id": "56764c7c-e0b8-4491-8dd2-9d46dab1c70b", "type": "concept", "title": "ILO standards"}, {"id": "8d122db5-21e0-4ebf-8bc7-12d140100a1b", "type": "concept", "title": "supplier codes"}, {"id": "fd0839ab-219e-49ef-8892-75a8768aacd9", "type": "concept", "title": "freedom of association"}, {"id": "994d6b70-7e54-48a5-86ee-ac1223f25fd6", "type": "concept", "title": "collective bargaining rights"}, {"id": "0636955a-2f1b-4f5e-902f-75948bff4462", "type": "concept", "title": "audits"}], "description": "Students learn how labor rights appear in global supply chains, trade rules, and corporate responsibility frameworks."}, {"id": "69dce953-94dc-42b0-92f5-7b44d2edc57a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multinational labor relations", "children": [{"id": "550d25dd-259b-427e-af4f-b175e5c64dae", "type": "concept", "title": "global framework agreements"}, {"id": "3621dd84-67e6-4b4d-94ac-21ffdac192fe", "type": "concept", "title": "European Works Councils"}, {"id": "d8e6bc97-7860-48a7-bb7a-f1f42be0172a", "type": "concept", "title": "cross-border campaigns"}, {"id": "fadc24aa-0815-4233-b34f-672a09659c45", "type": "concept", "title": "outsourcing"}, {"id": "0c7b3322-ce49-4e7f-92fd-25db09db2c11", "type": "concept", "title": "labor standards enforcement"}], "description": "The class considers how global employers and unions coordinate across legal systems and cultures."}]}, {"id": "b3cf9d1b-267f-415a-a5e6-e62a7abb5c3b", "type": "topic", "title": "Bargaining Simulation and Future of Labor Relations", "description": "The capstone turns the course into practice. Students prepare, bargain, draft settlement terms, reflect on strategy, and consider how labor relations is changing.", "children": [{"id": "0fe2fce3-00bb-4130-adc4-4d2bbe3bf027", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Simulation design and roles", "children": [{"id": "242872e1-6825-4767-9edf-62f2f1386105", "type": "concept", "title": "role assignments"}, {"id": "d7a6c71b-6a58-4566-91ed-2ad504b8ab9b", "type": "concept", "title": "confidential instructions"}, {"id": "d6b2d9f7-5d97-4be6-8374-7b00548e1835", "type": "concept", "title": "proposal packages"}, {"id": "51d30cc1-4652-423e-b501-d4f8c51f3028", "type": "concept", "title": "caucus discipline"}, {"id": "8468b66c-5084-4c83-9cab-38409841cd73", "type": "concept", "title": "settlement drafting"}], "description": "Students learn to use evidence, team roles, and negotiation discipline during a realistic bargaining exercise."}, {"id": "8960fc8e-63ba-4e26-9634-4a5c868a4c15", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Debrief and implementation", "children": [{"id": "5437be48-1c98-4dec-b94d-e1dfd76fda20", "type": "concept", "title": "debrief memos"}, {"id": "4a40be72-d346-4c2e-b060-6906685ee62e", "type": "concept", "title": "ratification strategy"}, {"id": "4b7c10f0-187a-4943-807e-be0753ea1a33", "type": "concept", "title": "implementation plan"}, {"id": "f5c58f85-f008-4ec3-89a0-76380c351392", "type": "concept", "title": "relationship repair"}, {"id": "a687c52b-1bea-4f96-a085-e4a3b59ac9cf", "type": "concept", "title": "lessons learned"}], "description": "The class examines what worked, what failed, and how a settlement would be communicated and administered."}, {"id": "5f3a0b75-6f54-4d96-91be-065a117e62d3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Future of worker voice", "children": [{"id": "203a683c-984e-463f-b1ae-4742b529f574", "type": "concept", "title": "platform work"}, {"id": "36c1adcd-da2a-4561-a8c1-af6aa05ed0ff", "type": "concept", "title": "minority unions"}, {"id": "3738ab32-0580-4378-9718-b7dc02ce6243", "type": "concept", "title": "remote organizing"}, {"id": "ac49043a-d8df-4745-87a3-343b8575ecf8", "type": "concept", "title": "AI management"}, {"id": "93bae0e3-3fcc-4d8d-91d3-b59caea8bfd9", "type": "concept", "title": "sectoral policy proposals"}], "description": "Students synthesize course themes through contemporary questions about gig work, remote work, AI, and new organizing models."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$lrcbjson$::jsonb,
