e communication"}], "description": "Students learn how automation, scheduling systems, AI, and restructuring become bargaining and implementation issues."}]}, {"id": "88935cfb-41fa-4e2c-b00c-6bcb987a00a5", "type": "topic", "title": "Comparative Labor Systems and Global Supply Chains", "description": "Students broaden their perspective by comparing U.S. labor relations with international and transnational models of worker representation.", "children": [{"id": "5a19c569-01e5-45fa-936b-46e27c530fb1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparative institutions", "children": [{"id": "90df4a53-6bd6-4d5b-9083-5d877d18a1c0", "type": "concept", "title": "sectoral bargaining"}, {"id": "9bd94091-fcb5-4fdd-8fb2-1dc3253475ac", "type": "concept", "title": "works councils"}, {"id": "fc1e0f6e-3920-4b3e-8a87-8f73feb9dcc1", "type": "concept", "title": "codetermination"}, {"id": "b1497960-ac93-4be8-ac9c-ace75b12e040", "type": "concept", "title": "social partnership"}, {"id": "05333efd-f184-4595-bf00-bfa3634022ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Ghent systems"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces institutions that differ from U.S. enterprise-level bargaining."}, {"id": "accb0eae-0fbc-4c63-9e25-d1f573f6aad1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global labor standards", "children": [{"id": "56764c7c-e0b8-4491-8dd2-9d46dab1c70b", "type": "concept", "title": "ILO standards"}, {"id": "8d122db5-21e0-4ebf-8bc7-12d140100a1b", "type": "concept", "title": "supplier codes"}, {"id": "fd0839ab-219e-49ef-8892-75a8768aacd9", "type": "concept", "title": "freedom of association"}, {"id": "994d6b70-7e54-48a5-86ee-ac1223f25fd6", "type": "concept", "title": "collective bargaining rights"}, {"id": "0636955a-2f1b-4f5e-902f-75948bff4462", "type": "concept", "title": "audits"}], "description": "Students learn how labor rights appear in global supply chains, trade rules, and corporate responsibility frameworks."}, {"id": "69dce953-94dc-42b0-92f5-7b44d2edc57a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multinational labor relati